course: dictionary
lesson: 14241
title: A formal word: necessitate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Necessitate is a formal word, the kind you find in official letters, reports and exam questions. It means to make something necessary, so that it has to happen or be done. «The heavy snow necessitated closing the road.» The snow made closing the road necessary, so nobody had a choice.
explain: Necessity means something you must have. To necessitate is to make that need appear. «The broken bridge necessitates a long detour.» The bridge is broken, so a long detour is needed. Ask yourself: what does this make necessary?
explain: Everyday speech uses simpler words. For «The damage necessitated repairs», you could say «The damage meant we needed repairs.» Put your easier words into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: Necessitate means to make something necessary or needed.
fact: It can also mean to force something to happen because there is no other way.
fact: Necessitate is a formal word, so you will find it in reports, letters and exam questions.
fact: «The damage necessitated repairs» means the damage made repairs needed.
fact: Simpler words with a similar meaning include need, require and force.
exercise: «Heavy snow necessitated closing the road.» What does necessitated mean here? | *Made closing the road necessary | Stopped the snow from falling | Cleared the road quickly | Made the road wider
exercise: «The broken bridge necessitates a long detour.» What is needed because of the broken bridge? | *A long detour | A swim in the river | A short walk across the river | A new bridge painted red
exercise: Mum says, «The lost key necessitates a call to the locksmith.» Which word means about the same as necessitates? | Forgets | Hides | *Requires | Decorates
test: «Running out of fuel necessitated an early landing.» What does this tell you? | The plane landed early for a party | *The plane had to land early because there was no other choice | The pilot wanted a longer flight | The fuel was extra and not needed
test: In a maths problem you read: «This plan necessitates twenty buses.» What does the question ask you to work out? | *How many buses are needed | How many people sit on one bus | How much each bus costs to paint | What colour the buses should be
exam: «The new rules necessitate a change to the school timetable.» In your own words, what does necessitate mean here? | The timetable is made of paper | The new rules are written in a book | *The new rules make a change to the timetable needed | The new rules remove the timetable completely
